# Bürglstein walkway (one-way; top 5 px = walking surface, the tile_steg
# deck so it lines up with steg and jetty): o lip, O planks with l joints,
# l underside, a d bearer, and one black iron knee bracket per tile (d strut
# with a k shadow edge) angled down-left to a d anchor plate with an i
# bolt, bolted into the rock. Behind the bracket the tile draws the cliff
# itself (tile_kalkfels_bg's fully joined frame: m with its d bedding), not
# transparency: a cell holds one tile, so a transparent felssteg would show
# the parallax layers as a stripe through the kalkfels_bg wall. Open
# ends get end grain (o lit left, l right) and a d end stanchion with a k
# shadow running down to the rock (the short handrail post would rise above
# the cell: a cell-top deck can't draw it). Only the left/right bits change
# the look. Generated by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids
# are the source.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_felssteg
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
